    "long_instructions": "## Optional Preview: Upcoming Level Tutorial\r\n\r\nIn the next level, you will create your first web app with HTML and the help of AI. This video walks through the steps to complete that. \r\n\r\nFeel free to watch as much or as little of the vidoe as you like. You can also refer back to it at any time. \r\n\r\n## Backpack Feature Support\r\n\r\nThe next level uses the **backpack feature**.\r\n\r\nThe backpack feature allows you to save and reuse code across different projects. Before you begin, you can expand the boxes below to preview how it works.\r\n\r\nYou don’t need to memorize these steps now. You can return to this page later if you need support.\r\n\r\n<details style=\"background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\">\r\n<summary style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;\">How to Save to the Backpack</summary>\r\n<div style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;\">\r\n\r\nStudents should get in the habit of saving their files after each level they build in it. This way, they can easily access the code on future projects. \r\n\r\n- Click the three-dot menu icon next to the `index.html` file name.\r\n- Select \"Save to backpack\" from the drop-down menu.\r\n- Name the file and press save.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/a5083c7ccc54bfa4ea561fa29adf2902-image-1740077664809.gif\" alt=\"gif of how to use the backpack\" width=\"650px\" style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\r\n\r\n</div></details>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Video Tutorial\r\n\r\nWant to see what’s coming next? Watch this quick tutorial for a step-by-step preview of the upcoming level.\r\n"
  },
